 "observations": [
  "The page number «213» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the right the number of the table, «Tab. 98», in bold sans serif, underlined. The page has no signature and no title: the folios of the manuscripts stand at the right above the double rule of the first field, in two lines of their own, «C 94r, O 149v,» and «N 60v.», the letters raised (L01-L02).",
  "The page holds three fields, as pp. 206-212 (JP2 0238-0244): «Viginti1) gradus Cancri» (L03), «Viginti quinque2) gradus Cancri» (L15) and «Triginta3) gradus Cancri» (L23), the ascendant at 20°, 25° and 30° of Cancer, with the numbers for the sextile, the quadrature and the trine (L04, L16, L24); headings and numbers in bold. The heads of the columns of the first field as on p. 212 (JP2 0244, L04-L07), from Cancer to Sagittarius, with «Horoscopus» in each and without notes (L05-L08). The second and the third field have no heads. Double rules divide the fields.",
  "The numbers of the three fields repeat those of the three fields of p. 212 (JP2 0244), for 5°, 10° and 15° of Cancer. The third field here (L25-L30) has all 72 numbers of the third field there (p. 212, L24-L29). The second has 62 of the 72 numbers of the second field there: its column of Cancer (5° 40′, 11° 23′, 17° 0′, 23° 0′, 29° 10′, 35° 18′) is that of the third field there, and it has 67° 7′ at 25° of Leo (L21) for 66° 7′ and 107° 38′ at 5° of Libra (L17) for 107° 58′. The first has 66 of the 72 numbers of the first field there, with 17° 8′ at 15° of Cancer (L11) for 17° 20′, 47° 37′ at 10° of Leo (L10) for 47° 57′, 75° 30′ at 5° of Virgo (L09) for 77° 30′, and at 20° of Libra, 25° and 30° of Sagittarius (L12-L14) 119° 38′, 178° 5′ and 183° 33′ for 119° 28′, 177° 5′ and 180° 33′, the readings that the first field there requires (p. 212, notes b and c and critical note AK07-CN235).",
  "The numbers at the head of a field, as on pp. 206-212 (JP2 0238-0244), are a third, a half and two thirds of one number, here not the last number of the field: in the first field 64° 25′, 96° 37′ and 128° 50′ (L04) belong to 193° 14′ to 193° 15′, where the field ends with 183° 33′ (L14); in the second the quadrature 97° 48′ and the trine 130° 24′ (L16) are a half and two thirds of 195° 36′, whose third is 65° 12′, where the sextile has 65° 42′, the third of 197° 6′, and the field ends with 185° 41′ (L22); in the third 65° 56′, 98° 55′ and 131° 52′ (L24) belong to 197° 48′ to 197° 50′, and the field ends with 189° 39′ (L30). These numbers continue those of p. 212 (JP2 0244), 183° 33′, 185° 41′ and 189° 40′ to 191° 39′ for 5°, 10° and 15° of Cancer.",
  "Notes on the readings. The edition's readings are those of the fields of p. 212 (JP2 0244): at 10° of Cancer in the first and the second field (notes b and e, L10, L18: the 11 of O and N against C's 9; 11° 10′ and 11° 23′), at 30° of Scorpius in the first (note c, L14: O's 153 against C's 154; 153° 48′), at 10° of Leo in the second (note f, L18: O's 47 against C's 48; 47° 43′) and at 15° of Libra in the third (note h, L27: C's 118 against O's 128; 118° 54′). The editor's corrections of the readings of all three manuscripts: the quadratures of the first and the second field (notes a and d, L04, L16: 96 for 66, half of 193° 14′ being 96° 37′; 97 for C's 72 and the 67 of O and N, half of 195° 36′ being 97° 48′), and at 15° of Leo in the second field (note g, L19: 53 for 54, 53° 55′ as on p. 212, JP2 0244, L18)."
